    "explanation" : "From [Effective Dart](https://dart.dev/guides/language/effective-dart/usage#dont-explicitly-initialize-variables-to-null):\n\n**DON'T** explicitly initialize variables to null.\n\nIn Dart, a variable or field that is not explicitly initialized automatically\ngets initialized to null.  This is reliably specified by the language.  There's\nno concept of \"uninitialized memory\" in Dart.  Adding `= null` is redundant and\nunneeded.\n\n**GOOD:**\n```dart\nint _nextId;\n\nclass LazyId {\n  int _id;\n\n  int get id {\n    if (_nextId == null) _nextId = 0;\n    if (_id == null) _id = _nextId++;\n\n    return _id;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**BAD:**\n```dart\nint _nextId = null;\n\nclass LazyId {\n  int _id = null;\n\n  int get id {\n    if (_nextId == null) _nextId = 0;\n    if (_id == null) _id = _nextId++;\n\n    return _id;\n  }\n}\n```",
